{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_30724f58bcce",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 9120,
      "mechanism": "The arbiter on each destination port indexes grant_encoded into the shared source-side bus using grant_encoded*S_COUNT+n. grant_encoded is a clog2(S_COUNT)-bit value from the arbiter's priority_encoder; S_COUNT (value 4) exceeds that index width, causing mux corruption and dropped valid. Changing the source-side stride M_COUNT->CL_M_COUNT at line 9113 aligns the multiplier to the arbiter's grant_encoded width, fixing the mux select for both cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_0551023abab5",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 12403,
      "mechanism": "The source-to-destination valid assignment int_axis_tvalid[m*M_COUNT +: M_COUNT] uses stride M_COUNT (value 1) instead of the destination count S_COUNT (value 4). This mis-indexes the shared valid bus so downstream arbiters read zeros. Changing the stride to CL_M_COUNT at line 12396 correctly maps each source's selected destination, enabling valid propagation at cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_35cdbadc2436",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 8726,
      "mechanism": "On rst the block-state drop_reg is not cleared. A leftover drop_reg=1 suppresses select_valid_next and forces int_s_axis_tready high, starving the arbiter of request assertions. Resetting drop_reg at line 8726 (inside the rst block) clears the stale drop so new transactions can acquire grants at cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_c1a2f86ca667",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 8726,
      "mechanism": "On rst the per-source select_reg is not cleared. A stale select_reg combined with a stale drop_reg causes the source ready logic to bypass the arbiter. Adding select_reg <= 0 at line 8726 (inside the rst block) ensures a clean selection state for the first grants at cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_61b4830137fb",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 11712,
      "mechanism": "The arbiter mux uses grant_encoded*S_COUNT for source indexing. With S_COUNT=4 this exceeds the grant_encoded width. Changing both source-side strides to CL_S_COUNT at lines 9113 and 11705 makes the multiplier match the encoder width, fixing the grant mux for cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_29a3f2743e76",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 11712,
      "mechanism": "The destination-side valid mux uses S_COUNT as stride for grant_encoded indexing. grant_encoded only has clog2(S_COUNT) bits; using S_COUNT overflows the index and reads wrong valid bits. Changing to CL_S_COUNT at line 11705 aligns the stride to the encoder width, restoring valid at cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_63dde08e3f82",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 12403,
      "mechanism": "The source-to-destination valid bus assignment uses M_COUNT as stride. For S_COUNT=4, M_COUNT=1 this places each source's valid in the wrong destination lane. Changing to S_COUNT at line 12396 maps each source to its selected destination, enabling m_axis_tvalid at cycles 4 and 5."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_cb1771b6727b",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 11712,
      "mechanism": "The arbiter mux on the destination side uses grant_encoded*S_COUNT to index source data, but grant_encoded width is clog2(S_COUNT). Changing the source-side multiplier to CL_S_COUNT at line 9113 and the destination-side multiplier to M_COUNT at line 11705 aligns both muxes to their respective index widths, fixing grant data selection for cycles 4 and 5."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The observed failure shows m_axis_tvalid stuck at 0 on cycles 4 and 5 while inputs are active. The datapath consists of per-source destination selection writing into a shared int_axis_tvalid bus (stride M_COUNT), then per-destination arbiters granting one source by grant_encoded and muxing with stride S_COUNT. The log indices reveal two complementary stride mismatches: (1) the source write uses M_COUNT (1) instead of the destination count, and (2) the arbiter mux uses S_COUNT (4) instead of its grant_encoded width clog2(S_COUNT). The highest-impact fixes correct these two strides with the clog2 parameters (CL_M_COUNT for the source write, CL_S_COUNT for the arbiter mux). A secondary cause is stale per-source block state (drop_reg, select_reg) not cleared on rst, which blocks the first grants. The top candidates therefore address the stride mismatches and the missing resets, each cited to its exact source line and the failing m_axis_tvalid port."
}
